{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Module.FiniteDimension","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Cone.InnerDual","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Dual","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.PiL2"],"declarations":29,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.farkas_alternative_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.farkas_alternative_real","kind":"theorem","line":535,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L535-L657","doc":"**The affine Farkas alternative** — the duality-shaped statement.\n\nIf the primal `{Ax = a, x ≥ 0}` is feasible and no feasible point has\nobjective below `γ`, then the dual `{lᵀA ≤ c}` has a point with\n`aᵀl ≥ γ`.\n\nThis is the statement `QOU.Optimization.MatrixFarkas` carries as its\nsingle field, unfolded. It is stated here without importing that module\nso this file stays Mathlib-shaped; the instance at `R = ℝ` is a\none-liner in a file that imports both.\n\n**No attainment is used.** The naive route — separating `(a, γ−ε)` from\nthe epigraph cone — yields `aᵀl > γ − ε` for every `ε` and never `≥ γ`.\nThis argues by contradiction on the *conclusion* instead: if the dual\nsystem is infeasible, `farkas_inequality` produces multipliers `(x, μ)`\nwith `Ax = μa` and `cᵀx < μγ`, and both branches of `μ` contradict the\nhypothesis directly. `μ > 0` rescales to a feasible point beating `γ`;\n`μ = 0` gives a recession direction along which the objective is\nunbounded below, so `x₀ + tx` beats `γ` for large `t`.\n\nThe primal-feasibility hypothesis is what makes the `μ = 0` branch\ncontradictory rather than merely uninformative — it supplies the `x₀`\nto move from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.farkas_inequality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.farkas_inequality","kind":"theorem","line":497,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L497-L526","doc":"**Farkas' lemma for a system of linear inequalities.**\n\nIf `Bl ≤ d` has no solution, there are non-negative multipliers `z`\nwith `Bᵀz = 0` and `dᵀz < 0` — a certificate of infeasibility.\n\nThis is the form the LP duality argument consumes. It follows from\n`farkas_vector` applied to `ineqGens B`: non-negativity on the basis\ngenerators gives `z ≥ 0`, non-negativity on **both** a column and its\nnegation forces the column pairing to vanish, and the strict inequality\nat `d` is `dᵀz < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.exists_solution_of_mem_coneSpan_ineqGens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.exists_solution_of_mem_coneSpan_ineqGens","kind":"theorem","line":470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L470-L495","doc":"**Membership in the cone exhibits a solution.** If `d` is a\nnon-negative combination of `ineqGens B`, then `Bl ≤ d` is solvable:\ntake `l` to be the difference of the two column blocks, and the basis\nblock is exactly the slack `d − Bl ≥ 0`.\n\nThis is the direction Farkas needs. Its contrapositive turns\n\"`Bl ≤ d` has no solution\" into \"`d` misses a closed cone\", which is\nwhat `farkas_vector` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ineqGens","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ineqGens","kind":"def","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L459-L468","doc":"Generators of `{Bl + s : l free, s ≥ 0} ⊆ ℝ^p`: the columns of `B`\nand their negations (letting `l` range over all signs), together with\nthe standard basis (the slack `s ≥ 0`). Finitely many, so the cone they\nspan is closed by `isClosed_coneSpan`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan_sum_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan_sum_apply","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L446-L457","doc":"Evaluating a combination coordinatewise.\n\nThe `show` is load-bearing: it re-elaborates the goal so that\n`Finset.sum_apply` matches. Without it the lemma does not fire at all —\n`EuclideanSpace` is a `WithLp` synonym, and while application reduces\ndefinitionally, `simp` will not see through the head symbol. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.farkas_vector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.farkas_vector","kind":"theorem","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L418-L436","doc":"**Farkas' lemma, vector form.**\n\nIf `b` is not a non-negative combination of `v`, there is a *vector* `z`\nwith `⟪z, vᵢ⟫ ≥ 0` for every generator and `⟪z, b⟫ < 0`.\n\nThis is `farkas_separation` pushed through Riesz representation. The\nfunctional form is the one separation produces; the vector form is the\none a linear program consumes, since dual feasibility `Aᵀl ≤ c` is a\nstatement about a vector of multipliers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.euclidean_inner_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.euclidean_inner_eq","kind":"theorem","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L412-L416","doc":"The real inner product on `EuclideanSpace` in coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.nonneg_on_coneSpan_of_nonneg_on_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.nonneg_on_coneSpan_of_nonneg_on_generators","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L392-L401","doc":"The converse half of the alternative, for completeness: a functional\nnon-negative on the generators is non-negative on the cone, so the two\nalternatives of `farkas_separation` are mutually exclusive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.farkas_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.farkas_separation","kind":"theorem","line":373,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L373-L389","doc":"**Farkas' lemma**, in separating-functional form.\n\nIf `b` is not a non-negative combination of `v`, then some continuous\nlinear functional is non-negative on every generator and strictly\nnegative at `b`. Exactly one of the two alternatives holds — the\nconverse direction is immediate, since a functional non-negative on the\ngenerators is non-negative on the whole cone.\n\nThis is what `isClosed_coneSpan` was for: `ProperCone.hyperplane_separation`\nneeds a *closed* cone, and closedness of a finitely generated cone is\nprecisely the fact Mathlib was missing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coe_coneSpanProper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coe_coneSpanProper","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L369-L371","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanProper","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanProper","kind":"def","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L363-L367","doc":"`coneSpan` as a **proper** cone — the packaging `isClosed_coneSpan`\nmakes available, and the form Mathlib's separation theorem consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coe_coneSpanPointed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coe_coneSpanPointed","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L359-L361","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanPointed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanPointed","kind":"def","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L344-L356","doc":"`coneSpan` as a pointed cone: it contains `0` and is closed under\naddition and non-negative scaling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.mem_coneSpan_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.mem_coneSpan_generator","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L338-L342","doc":"Each generator lies in the cone it generates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_coneSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_coneSpan","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L319-L329","doc":"**A finitely generated cone is closed.**\n\nThe gap `qou/kl8z` identifies as the single analytic input to the whole\nLP layer. Modulo `exists_linearIndependent_support`, which is finite and\nalgebraic, this is now derived: the cone is a *finite* union of sub-cones\non independent subfamilies, and each of those is closed by\n`isClosed_coneSpan_of_linearIndependent`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan_eq_iUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan_eq_iUnion","kind":"theorem","line":305,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L305-L317","doc":"The cone is the union of the sub-cones on independent subfamilies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.exists_linearIndependent_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.exists_linearIndependent_support","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L293-L303","doc":"Conic Carathéodory, in the form the union decomposition needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_coneSpanOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_coneSpanOn","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L191-L195","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanOn_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanOn_eq","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L176-L189","doc":"A sub-cone is the cone on the corresponding subfamily. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_eq_sum_subtype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_eq_sum_subtype","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L170-L174","doc":"A sum over `ι` of something supported in `s` is a sum over `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanOn_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanOn_subset","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L164-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpanOn","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L159-L161","doc":"The sub-cone using only the generators indexed by `s`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_coneSpan_of_linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_coneSpan_of_linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L140-L149","doc":"**A cone on linearly independent generators is closed.**\n\nThe coefficient map is injective and its domain is finite-dimensional,\nso it is a closed embedding; the cone is the image of the closed\nnon-negative orthant under it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.ker_coneMap_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.ker_coneMap_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L131-L138","doc":"`coneMap` is injective exactly when the generators are independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_nonneg_orthant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.isClosed_nonneg_orthant","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L117-L123","doc":"The non-negative orthant is closed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan_eq_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan_eq_image","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L106-L114","doc":"`coneSpan` is the image of the non-negative orthant under `coneMap`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneMap_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneMap_apply","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L102-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneMap","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L92-L100","doc":"The coefficient map `x ↦ Σᵢ xᵢ vᵢ`, as a linear map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.coneSpan","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/FinitelyGeneratedConeClosed.lean#L87-L90","doc":"The cone generated by a finite family: all non-negative combinations\nof `v`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}